data the_seed_accepts_an_expr_error_node_and_the_emitter_writes_a_panic: RecurringFailureMode = RecurringFailureMode {
  identity: "the_seed_accepts_an_expr_error_node_and_the_emitter_writes_a_panic" as NonEmptyStr,

  rung: RungUnread { cause: NoRungStated },

  receipts: [
    "MECHANISM: the fail-open is that re-inference (v1.compiler.infer, ExprError arm) diagnoses ONLY kind CensusHeadsBodyStripped and answers [] for every other kind, so no error node but that one ever stops the compile. INVALID STATE: the v1 seed ACCEPTS a program that contains an ExprError node (v1.compiler.core make_expr_error_node, kind SemanticExprError), and the emitter writes it into the generated program as a runtime panic. v1.compiler.infer re-inference of an ExprError node answers no diagnostic for any kind but CensusHeadsBodyStripped, so a node minted by the field-access cascade arm (message 'error type cascade', occurrence OccurrenceSynthetic) carries no diagnostic of its own; v1.compiler.emit emit_error_expr (called from emit_simple_expr and the main expression arm) renders it through language_spec(target).error_expr_template, which for Rust is extdeps.languages.rust.emit rust_error_expr_template = panic!({0}). The panic text is the symptom; the defect is that compilation succeeded. REFUSAL BELONGS AT THE FIRST ERROR NODE, at compile time, located at its span (DESIGN 5: a wrong answer is a loud error, never fabricated output).",

    "SPECIMEN, found 2026-11-05 (gunbc#15612, royal-seal-647): once a type declaration's fields resolve under its own parameters, a field access whose base expanded to a CompilerError took the cascade arm and the seed emitted panic!(\"error type cascade\") in place of the expression; only rustc's unreachable-code lint caught it downstream. The FIRST error node's origin (the base's own CompilerError) is a separate link, still under read; this row is the fail-open at the consumer end and holds whatever that origin turns out to be.",

    "CEILING NOT YET STATED: the renderer is read (emit_error_expr and its two callers); whether any ExprError kind is legitimately emitted by a declared route (CensusHeadsBodyStripped is the one kind with a diagnostic) is unread, so the attainable rung is not derived. NEXT TRIGGER: read every make_expr_error_node site (04_infer, 04_resolve) and classify each as diagnosed or silent."
  ],

  evidence: [],
}
